{
  // DueJob
  // A self-describing maintenance box. The box itself states when it is next due and what it pays,
  // so any executor — a Lithos miner inside its own block, or anyone else — can advance it with no
  // knowledge of any protocol beyond this script. It is the reference job of the client's upkeep
  // source.

  // THE RULE, IN WORDS
  // The box is due once HEIGHT reaches the last beat (R4) plus the period (R5); the sum is taken in
  // Long, so a period near the Int maximum makes a box that is never due rather than one that fails
  // to evaluate; either way such a box never advances. A spend of a due box must
  // recreate it as OUTPUTS(0): the same script, the same tokens, R4 set to this block's height, R5
  // and R6 unchanged, a creation height of this block, and a value of at least the box's value less
  // the tip (R6). The box must be INPUTS(0), so one transaction advances at most one due-job box
  // (its other inputs are unconstrained): two boxes with the same terms cannot share one successor
  // while the spender keeps the second whole. The period must
  // be positive and the tip not negative, or the box never advances. Whatever the successor does not
  // keep, which is at most the tip, is unconstrained: whoever builds the spend directs it.
  // The fresh creation height is what makes a beat reset the storage-rent clock: a successor stamped
  // with an old height would be as close to rent as the box it replaced. Because R4 and the creation
  // height must both equal HEIGHT, a beat transaction is valid at exactly one height and can never be
  // included later; and a late beat moves the schedule, since the next due height counts from the
  // beat, not from when the box was due.

  // REGISTERS
  // R4 Int   height of the last beat; the box is due at R4 + R5, computed in Long
  // R5 Int   period, in blocks; must be positive
  // R6 Long  tip per beat, in nanoERG; must not be negative
  // A box whose registers are missing or of other types cannot be spent under this script at all
  // (`R4[Int].get` on a Long fails), so it is locked until storage rent takes it. So is a box funded
  // at exactly its own minimum with a small R4 or creation height: the successor's R4 and creation
  // height take more bytes at today's height, so it needs more value than the box holds and no
  // keyless executor can add any; and a box within a few bytes of the 4,096-byte box limit, whose
  // successor would grow past it.

  // HOW THE BOX ENDS
  // There is no owner and no exit path; the box is keyless end to end. The successor must keep at
  // least value - R6, and `>=` lets it keep more: an executor may take a smaller tip, or none, and a
  // beat for free is valid. So a box lives as long as anyone beats it, whether or not it can still
  // pay, and ages out through storage rent only when it is left alone. A creator funds it for the
  // tips wanted and walks away. Tokens stay with the box through every beat and leave it only with
  // storage rent. A tip at or above the box's value means the creator offered the whole box: the
  // successor need keep nothing the script asks for, only what consensus asks of any box.
  //
  // WHAT THE SCRIPT LEAVES FREE
  // Only OUTPUTS(0)'s script, tokens, R4 to R6, creation height and value are constrained. Its R7 to
  // R9, every other output, the other inputs and the data inputs are free: an executor may attach
  // registers to the successor, raising its minimum value (a later beat may drop them, as the
  // reference job does, or keep them), and may put the tip anywhere, including a fee. The standing
  // box's own R4 is not checked either: a creator's R4 above the current height delays the first
  // beat until R4 + R5. `onlyOne` binds only boxes at this exact tree.

  // ASSUMPTIONS
  // None. The contract takes no compile-time constants; it reads SELF, OUTPUTS(0) and INPUTS(0)'s
  // id, and no data input.

  val successor = OUTPUTS(0)
  val lastBeat  = SELF.R4[Int].get
  val period    = SELF.R5[Int].get
  val tip       = SELF.R6[Long].get

  val sane        = period > 0 && tip >= 0L
  val onlyOne     = INPUTS(0).id == SELF.id
  val due         = HEIGHT.toLong >= lastBeat.toLong + period.toLong
  val sameScript  = successor.propositionBytes == SELF.propositionBytes
  val sameTokens  = successor.tokens == SELF.tokens
  val beatStamped = successor.R4[Int].get == HEIGHT
  val freshStamp  = successor.creationInfo._1 == HEIGHT
  val periodKept  = successor.R5[Int].get == period
  val tipKept     = successor.R6[Long].get == tip
  val valueKept   = successor.value >= SELF.value - min(tip, SELF.value)

  sigmaProp(sane && onlyOne && due && sameScript && sameTokens && beatStamped && freshStamp &&
    periodKept && tipKept && valueKept)
}
